  <ym-title|Finite-volume probe assembly><label|finite-volume-probe-assembly>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, trace selected-scale producer.

    <item>Status: draft; review requested; the assembly is conditional on the
    explicitly displayed paid-component and buffered-chamber estimates.

    <item>Imported Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-probe-assembly.tex>.

    <item>Scope: reconstructs the mathematical proof of the central
    finite-dimensional assembly performed by the selected <verbatim|tide>
    producer: two paid local components and the buffered chamber estimate
    yield the complete coefficient/parity/toll data of a probe. It does not
    claim to produce the paid components, Bill receipts, or Crown/stage-Crown
    buffer.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  item>>|<cell|<strong|Exact source>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence/status>>>|<row|<cell|Full
  probe target and assembly>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Glade.tide>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Grid.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|tide>
  outputs a probe at grade five from two local films, two coefficient labels,
  Bill receipts, room/interiority, and a Crown receipt for the symmetrized
  small field. The manuscript proves the three output components
  explicitly.>>|<row|<cell|Probe fields>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Probe>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Meteor.lean>>|<cell|The target has
  coefficient cost, central signed-inversion oddness, an interior root-error
  witness, and a separated two-site bound against every bounded interior test
  in the specified window/room. The manuscript states those mathematical
  properties.>>|<row|<cell|Paid component and
  rate>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Bill>, <verbatim|.root>,
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.tends_price>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Casa.lean>,
  <verbatim|CabinBook.lean>, <verbatim|Cabin.lean>>|<cell|Each Bill
  coefficient has size at most one; its root error after the required scale
  transport is bounded by <verbatim|nativeC>; <verbatim|tends_price> proves
  the selected paid quantity is at most <verbatim|Tau(j,-430)>. The
  manuscript uses the exact resulting inequalities (15) rather than treating
  a Bill record name as proof.>>|<row|<cell|Chamber
  buffer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Crown>, <verbatim|.stageCrown>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Crown.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Crown.cost>
  supplies a chamber approximation and very small root cost;
  <verbatim|stageCrown> upgrades this to a two-site price at most
  <verbatim|Tau(i,-30000)> against any test bounded by
  <verbatim|Tau(i,150000)>, interior to the grade-four window, and within
  room. The manuscript states this upgraded bound as (16), and records its
  producer as outside the assembly scope.>>|<row|<cell|Scale, response, and
  symmetry identities>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Glade.tide>, helpers
  <verbatim|linC>, <verbatim|toss>, <verbatim|stroll>, <verbatim|weighing>,
  <verbatim|readY>, <verbatim|readUp>, <verbatim|prelude>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/{Grid,Trail}.lean>>|<cell|These
  identities show that finite observation is linear, commutes with
  signed-motion averaging, scales through the degree-five dilation, and that
  chamber pullback commutes with the finite motion sum. The manuscript writes
  these identities as (12) and uses termwise expansion.>>|<row|<cell|Finite
  averaging and coefficient cost>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Prism>,
  <verbatim|.Reed>, <verbatim|.blade>, <verbatim|.blade_cost>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Turf.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Motion>
  is the product of signed permutations and an independent conjugation bit.
  <verbatim|Prism> is its real-linear coefficient action; <verbatim|Reed>
  averages with weights <verbatim|rent*hued>, where
  <verbatim|hued(s,d)=sign(s,prev(s,d))> and
  <verbatim|prev(s,d)=s.perm\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>(d)>. The proof of
  covariance reindexes by <verbatim|splitP> and uses <verbatim|prev_step> and
  <verbatim|hue_step>, yielding <verbatim|rho_g Z_d=sign(g,d) Z_(g.perm(d))>;
  reality reindexes by <verbatim|dualP> and uses <verbatim|shield>.
  <verbatim|blade> proves the resulting signed-covariant reality condition,
  and <verbatim|frames_night> gives <verbatim|rho_archV Z_d=\<minus\>Z_d> for
  each component. <verbatim|blade_cost> bounds the transported column size by
  <verbatim|orbitCost> times the maximal input size. <verbatim|prelude>
  proves column-map real-linearity and covariance; <verbatim|majesty>
  supplies the transported bound 2 from each paid <verbatim|Bill> label. The
  manuscript writes the finite reindexing and norm
  argument.>>|<row|<cell|Root averaging and
  interior>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.teamW>, <verbatim|.reedRoad>,
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Broom>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Trail.lean>,
  <verbatim|Grid.lean>>|<cell|On the chamber-interior class, the finite seam
  gives signed-motion invariance and triangle inequality for the root
  seminorm. <verbatim|Broom>, <verbatim|reedRoad>, and <verbatim|teamW>
  establish chamber/window interiority and preserve a common root estimate
  under the normalized signed sum. The manuscript requires precisely this
  interior domain before applying those inequalities.>>|<row|<cell|Scale
  arithmetic>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.tide>,
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Tau_add>, <verbatim|.toll_small>,
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.tends_price>; <verbatim|Grid.lean>,
  <verbatim|Arms.lean>, <verbatim|Cabin.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|tide> uses
  <verbatim|beta\<leq\>2 betaHat(k)>, <verbatim|betaHat(k)\<geq\>1>,
  <verbatim|1+2 betaHat(k)\<leq\>Tau(j,230)>, and <verbatim|6
  orbitCost\<leq\>betaHat(k)>. The last two bounds arise from the selected
  rate-ticket/growth receipts; <verbatim|Tau(230) Tau(-430)=Tau(-200)>. For
  coefficient cost, <verbatim|(2+2 beta) orbitCost\<leq\>6 orbitCost
  betaHat(k)\<leq\>betaHat(k)^2\<leq\>a^5 betaHat(k)^4>.>>>>>

  <section|Route to the public mission><label|route-to-the-public-mission>

  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Slate.hullage>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Phantom.lean>,
  invokes <verbatim|YM.Trace.Weir.crestship> at fixed cover parameter 48 and
  builds <verbatim|Mission> with fixed probe complexity 4. The core marker is
  the grade-five projection of the signed-orbit transform of the selected
  field difference. The proof of <verbatim|crestship> invokes this probe
  assembly after producing the two Bill decompositions and the Crown data.
  The detailed production of those paid components and buffered chamber
  estimate is not discharged in this unit; they remain explicit upstream
  construction work.

  <section|Commands and checks><label|commands-and-checks>

  Read-only source inspection used <verbatim|rg -n> and <verbatim|sed -n> on
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/{Grid,Trail,Turf,Crown,Casa,Cabin,Arms,Meteor}.lean>,
  plus <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Phantom.lean>. No Lean source
  was edited. No TeX, Lean, or test build was run. Blueprint validation has
  not been run on this new evidence file.

